WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:03.190
Enceladus, spraying its ocean into space.

00:03.890 --> 00:12.874
Cassini found the jets in 2005, coming off the south pole at four hundred metres a second, and flew straight through them.

00:13.324 --> 00:24.727
They carry water, salt, silica and more organic material than anyone expected, and they have not stopped: the dust keeps one of Saturn's outer rings supplied.
